      "id": 132943,
      "name": "Silverleaf",
      "username": "Silverleaf",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-21T20:16:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Corvids are awesome.</p><p>The one time I visited the Tower of London I watched one of the ravens sneak up on a man who was eating a sandwich. Once the man turned around and I swear the raven looked away all nonchalant until he turned back again, concentrating on his sandwich, chatting to his family.</p><p>The raven bided its time, waiting for the perfect moment, creeping ever closer. With an almost silent flap of its clipped wings, it hopped onto the back of the man's bench, still undetected. Then in one swift move it made a grab for the sandwich and legged it over the low humans-are-not-allowed-in-here fence with its prize.</p><p>It was a beautiful moment, and although I managed to restrain myself so I only laughed a little bit I was cheering that raven on inside. Especially awesome was the \"please don't feed the ravens\" sign on the fence...</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:08:31.266Z",
