      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"Mezike\"]\n\nWhat about baby Ravens? Can they pass the test? \n[/quote]\n \n\n Haven&#39;t seen any research on them, but if my own anecdotal evidence of baby magpies means anything, I&#39;d have to say probably not. \n\n I made a hedgehog feeding station in my garden one summer, using an old guinea pig run propped up so hedgehogs could get underneath to get to the cat food I left there, but foxes and cats couldn&#39;t. Every morning I had to rescue a pair of young magpies who were smart enough to spot the food and get in there, but panicked when they couldn&#39;t find the exit. No adult birds though, so draw your own conclusions. \n\n Also ravens and magpies can learn to talk really well. That is awesome. \n",
